---
title: GraphQL API
description: Schema, queries, and mutations for Contacts, OAuth Clients, Client Databases, and Refresh Tokens.
---

Endpoint: `POST /graphql` (requires `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`).
A GraphQL Playground is available at `/playground` (no auth, dev convenience).

The schema is defined in `schema/*.graphql` (SDL), generated into Go via
`gqlgen` (`schema/gqlgen.yml`, see [development](/docs/api/development)).
Resolvers live in `gql/resolvers/`.

---

## Contacts (`schema/Contacts.graphql`)

Versioned per-user address-book entries. Follows the project's
[versioning pattern](/docs/api/data-model#versioning-pattern)
(`contact` / `contact_version` / `derived_from`).

```graphql
type Contact {
  id: ID!
  name: String!
  email: String!
  phone: String
  created_at: String!
  updated_at: String!
}

type ContactVersion {
  id: ID!
  contact_id: ID!
  name: String!
  email: String!
  phone: String
  created_at: String!
}

input ContactVersionFilter {
  name: String
  email: String
  phone: String
  before: String
}

input CreateContactInput {
  name: String!
  email: String!
  phone: String
}

input UpdateContactInput {
  name: String
  email: String
  phone: String
}
```

### Queries

| Query | Description |
|---|---|
| `contacts(limit: Int, offset: Int): [Contact!]!` | Lists the caller's contacts. Default limit 50. |
| `contact(id: ID!): Contact` | Fetches a single contact, scoped to the caller. |
| `contactHistory(id: ID!, filter: ContactVersionFilter): [ContactVersion!]!` | Full version history, optionally filtered by field values or a `before` timestamp. |

### Mutations

| Mutation | Description |
|---|---|
| `createContact(input: CreateContactInput!): Contact!` | Creates a contact owned by the caller. |
| `updateContact(id: ID!, parentVersionIds: [ID!]!, input: UpdateContactInput!): Contact!` | Updates a contact, creating a new `contact_version`. `parentVersionIds` records ancestry (1 entry for a normal edit, 2 for a merge of diverging histories). |
| `deleteContact(id: ID!): Boolean!` | Deletes a contact owned by the caller. |

**Auth:** All operations resolve the caller's user ID from the JWT subject
(`middleware.ClaimFromContext(ctx).Subject`) and scope reads/writes to that
user — contacts are private per-user.

---

## OAuth Clients (`schema/Clients.graphql`)

Admin API for managing third-party OAuth clients (the OAuth "applications"
that can request tokens from this server).

```graphql
type OAuthClient {
  id: ID!
  scopes: [String!]!          # scopes this client may request
  redirect_uris: [String!]!
  public: Boolean!            # true = PKCE-only, no client secret
  auto_grant_scopes: Boolean!  # true = consent screen skipped
}

type CreateClientResult {
  client: OAuthClient!
  secret: String              # null for public clients; shown once
}

input CreateClientInput {
  id: String!                 # used as OAuth client_id AND SurrealDB record key; must be unique
  redirect_uris: [String!]!
  scopes: [String!]!
  auto_grant_scopes: Boolean   # skip consent for first-party apps
  public: Boolean              # true = PKCE-only client, no secret generated
}
```

### Queries

| Query | Description |
|---|---|
| `clients(limit: Int, offset: Int): [OAuthClient!]!` | Lists registered OAuth clients. Default limit 50. |
| `oauthClient(id: ID!): OAuthClient` | Fetches a single client by ID. |

### Mutations

| Mutation | Description |
|---|---|
| `createClient(input: CreateClientInput!): CreateClientResult!` | Creates a confidential client (32-byte random secret, returned once, stored as a bcrypt hash) or, if `public: true`, a PKCE-only client with no secret. |
| `deleteClient(id: ID!): Boolean!` | Deletes a client and its associated records. |

**Note:** `createClient` does **not** provision a per-client database — that
is a separate, opt-in step (see ClientDatabases below).

---

## ClientDatabases (`schema/ClientDatabases.graphql`)

Lets an OAuth client provision its own isolated SurrealDB database(s) — up
to **5 per client** — with an optional custom schema applied as DDL.
Provisioning emits a `billing_provisioning_event`.

```graphql
type ClientDatabase {
  id: ID!
  client_id: ID!
  name: String!       # caller-chosen label, must match ^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$
  db_name: String!    # actual provisioned SurrealDB database name
  status: String!     # "active" | "suspended" | "deleted"
  created_at: String!
  updated_at: String!
}

type CreateClientDatabaseResult {
  database: ClientDatabase!
  db_password: String!  # generated DB user password — shown once, store securely
}

input FieldDefInput {
  name: String!
  type: String!  # base: string,int,float,decimal,bool,datetime,duration,bytes,uuid,object,any
                  # parameterized: option<T>, array<T>, set<T> (recursive)
}

input IndexDefInput {
  name: String!
  fields: [String!]!
  unique: Boolean
}

input TableDefInput {
  name: String!
  schemafull: Boolean
  fields: [FieldDefInput!]
  indexes: [IndexDefInput!]
}

input DatabaseSchemaInput {
  tables: [TableDefInput!]!
}
```

### Queries

| Query | Description |
|---|---|
| `clientDatabases(clientId: ID!): [ClientDatabase!]!` | Lists non-deleted databases for a client, oldest first. |

### Mutations

| Mutation | Description |
|---|---|
| `createClientDatabase(clientId: ID!, name: String!, schema: DatabaseSchemaInput): CreateClientDatabaseResult!` | Provisions a new SurrealDB database for the client (rejects if the client already has 5). Validates `name`. If `schema` is given, generates and applies `DEFINE TABLE` / `DEFINE FIELD` / `DEFINE INDEX` DDL. Returns the new DB's name and a one-time password. |
| `updateClientDatabaseSchema(clientId: ID!, name: String!, schema: DatabaseSchemaInput!): ClientDatabase!` | Applies additional/updated DDL to an existing client database and stores the new `schema_def`. |

**Implementation note:** the resolver (`gql/resolvers/ClientDatabases.resolvers.go`)
is hand-maintained (not gqlgen-regenerated) and owns all logic — quota
check, name/type validation, DDL generation, billing — inline. The store
(`storage/database/surreal.go`) only exposes the two operations that need
admin DB credentials: `ProvisionClientDatabase` and `ApplyDDLToClientDB`.

---

## RefreshTokens (`schema/RefreshTokens.graphql`)

Lets clients/users inspect and revoke issued refresh tokens.

```graphql
type RefreshToken {
  id: ID!
  client: OAuthClient!
  scopes: [String!]!
  expires_at: String!
  created_at: String!
  revoked: Boolean!
  used: Boolean!
}
```

### Queries

| Query | Description |
|---|---|
| `refreshTokens(limit: Int, offset: Int): [RefreshToken!]!` | Lists refresh tokens. Default limit 50. |

### Mutations

| Mutation | Description |
|---|---|
| `revokeRefreshToken(id: ID!): Boolean!` | Revokes a refresh token (and its underlying grant). |

**Auth (scope-gated):**
- `tokens:read` — caller may list/revoke only their **own** tokens (results
  filtered to the caller's user ID, optionally a specific client).
- `tokens:all:read` — caller may list/revoke **any** user's tokens.
- The `client` field is lazily resolved from the linked `oauth_client`
  record only if requested.
